---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('activecampaign')!;
const b = appBySlug('justuno')!;
const path = '/compare/activecampaign-vs-justuno';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-justuno');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-justuno');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Are these interchangeable cart senders?",
    "answer": "No. Evaluate ActiveCampaign for Shopify cart-triggered email and Justuno for onsite capture and its handoff to a connected platform."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a Justuno signup prove abandonment?",
    "answer": "No. Keep signup identity and permission separate from the Shopify cart event and the sender\u2019s eligibility checks."
  },
  {
    "question": "What happens to missed cart events after a sync?",
    "answer": "ActiveCampaign documents that missed abandoned carts synced afterward do not trigger automations. Reconcile current state before deciding how to handle an outage."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are the schedules and margin examples tested results?",
    "answer": "No supplier test is reported. Margin examples assume fixed product costs; proposed workflow checks must be performed in the merchant\u2019s own setup."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <a href="/compare" class="link text-sm font-bold">← Comparisons</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-6">ActiveCampaign vs Justuno: sending or onsite capture?</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">These products address different parts of recovery. Decide whether the missing capability is a sender workflow or a better handoff from onsite capture.</p>
    <TldrBox picks={[{ label: "Evaluate", tool: a.name, reason: "Shopify cart-triggered email automation" },{ label: "Context", tool: b.name, reason: "Onsite signup and handoff to a connected platform" }]} />
    <div class="mt-12 card overflow-x-auto"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>{a.name}</th><th>{b.name}</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Responsibility</td><td>Shopify cart-triggered email automation</td><td>Onsite signup and handoff to a connected platform</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Evidence to inspect</td><td>Deep Data event and automated email content</td><td>Captured fields, destination list and permission mapping</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Combined setup</td><td>Own send eligibility and exits</td><td>Own form targeting and successful delivery of signup data</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Choose the missing responsibility</h2>
      <p>ActiveCampaign documents Shopify abandoned-cart email automation through its integration. Justuno’s ActiveCampaign integration documentation describes syncing new signups to a selected list; that page is explicitly labelled legacy. Confirm the setup for your current Justuno version. A successful signup sync does not establish cart tracking, purchase suppression or permission for every sending channel.</p>
      <h2>ActiveCampaign: validate the Shopify trigger</h2>
      <p>Connect the supported Shopify integration and inspect the Abandons Cart trigger and abandoned-cart content block. The Shopify integration has an abandonment wait setting; include it when reasoning about total elapsed time rather than adding an arbitrary reminder delay to an unknown clock. Confirm the correct store, currency, cart items and destination link on a test contact.</p>
      <h2>Justuno: validate the capture handoff</h2>
      <p>Submit a form with a fresh email address and known field values. Check destination list, custom-field mapping, permission evidence and the time the receiving system gets the signup. Repeat with an existing unsubscribed profile and a failed integration request. Decide who owns retries and deduplication; never turn a retry into a second welcome or a renewed subscription without appropriate permission.</p>
      <h2>When both belong in the stack</h2>
      <p>Use onsite capture to address a visitor-identification or form-targeting problem and a connected sender to manage later messages. A form submit is not proof that a cart was abandoned. Join identities carefully, keep the Shopify cart event separate, and assign one sender queue owner. Before sending, recheck purchase, stock, suppression, channel permission and quiet hours. SMS or push suggestions require separate verified sending support.</p>
      <h2>Model the offer before automating it</h2>
      <p>These are illustrative calculations, not supplier results. A $644 cart at 63% gross margin has fixed product cost $238.28 and full-price gross profit $405.72. An 8% code leaves $592.48 revenue and $354.20 gross profit, losing $51.52 before other costs. A $479 cart at 37% with a 13% code leaves $114.96 rather than $177.23 gross profit. Resolve shipping, bundle or subscription confusion before assuming an incentive is needed.</p>
      <h2>Proposed acceptance and outage checks</h2>
      <p>Test a captured signup with no cart, a cart that reaches checkout, and a purchase while a reminder waits. The first should not become a fabricated abandonment event; the others should demonstrate correct eligibility and exits. During an integration interruption, retain event identifiers and reconcile purchase and suppression state before replay. ActiveCampaign’s documentation says missed abandoned carts synced afterward do not trigger automations; do not promise automatic recovery of every missed send.</p>
      <h2>Judge the combined cost and ownership</h2>
      <p>Compare the sender cost plus any capture subscription and integration work for the same audience and traffic. Measure completed signups separately from eligible cart events and incremental purchases. A randomized holdout can help estimate incrementality when sample size permits; choose its size from the traffic and uncertainty you can support. Neither popup conversion nor platform-attributed revenue alone establishes profitable recovery.</p>
      <h2>Documentation checked November 25, 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001045964-Abandoned-cart-overview">ActiveCampaign abandoned cart overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000202150-Connect-your-Shopify-store-to-ActiveCampaign">ActiveCampaign Shopify settings and sync behavior</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.justuno.com/article/918-active-campaign-integration">Justuno legacy ActiveCampaign integration</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
